Legal element Construct to measure Design requirement
Appreciable impairment (AI Act 5(1)(a)) Decision quality: understanding of material characteristics, costs and risks Direct measurement, not proxy constructs such as decision confidence alone
Decision the person would not otherwise have made Preference stability: consistency after neutral information and time for reflection Pre–post comparison; post-cooling-off revision reported as confounded by the withdrawal right, not as primary evidence
