These appendices are offered in the same conditional register as the main text. The DFA is a proposal in the preparatory phase; the Parliament and Council may alter the vulnerability concept, the certainty standards, or the evidence-shifting powers. The empirical protocol is pre-registrable but not executed, and its construct validity is bounded as stated. The value of the appendices is not that they settle the questions, but that they make the questions operational—so that the final legislative text and the executed experiment can each confirm or reject the specific claims the thesis advances.

